        <name>Vars</name>
        <qualifiedname>LiveDebugValues::VLocTracker::Vars</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Map <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_debug_variable" kindref="compound">DebugVariable</ref> to the latest <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_value" kindref="compound">Value</ref> it&apos;s defined to have. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Needs to be a <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_map_vector" kindref="compound">MapVector</ref> because we determine order-in-the-input-MIR from the order in this container. (FIXME: likely no longer true as the ordering is now provided by <ref refid="class_live_debug_values_1_1_debug_variable_map" kindref="compound">DebugVariableMap</ref>). We only retain the last <ref refid="class_live_debug_values_1_1_dbg_value" kindref="compound">DbgValue</ref> in each block for each variable, to determine the blocks live-out variable value. The Vars container forms the transfer function for this block, as part of the dataflow analysis. The movement of values between locations inside of a block is handled at a much later stage, in the <ref refid="class_transfer_tracker" kindref="compound">TransferTracker</ref> class. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
